{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116482",
      "title": "Making Sense of The CanDeactivate Guard",
      "lectureOrder": 298,
      "videoOrder": 283,
      "sourceHash": "65db32d031e09a1e773f90e0e186f2579faa2cfbbb66be23ee92ac93912b9e3d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "The idea behind can deactivate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 6.18,
          "en": "is that you can control whether a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.18,
          "end": 9.21,
          "en": "is allowed to leave a page or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.21,
          "end": 12.9,
          "en": "Now to show you how the can deactivate route guard works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 15.96,
          "en": "I'll go to that new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.96,
          "end": 20.04,
          "en": "And then there in this file, below this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 25.04,
          "en": "I'll export a new constant called can leave edit page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 28.08,
          "en": "or however you wanna name it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.08,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "which should be of type can deactivate FN.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 34.35,
          "en": "And then that will be a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.35,
          "end": 38.04,
          "en": "that receives information about the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.04,
          "end": 40.683,
          "en": "you're trying to leave as a first argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.67,
          "end": 44.1,
          "en": "Though you should add angle brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 48.66,
          "en": "to let TypeScript know to which component this will be tied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.66,
          "end": 52.86,
          "en": "So here you should insert your component class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.86,
          "end": 55.95,
          "en": "new task component in my case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.95,
          "end": 57.84,
          "en": "And that's then what will get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.84,
          "end": 59.82,
          "en": "as a first input parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.82,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "The component instance which we're trying to leave.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "And you then also could accept a couple of other parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "with information about the current route, the current state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 73.26,
          "en": "of the router, and the next state that is expected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.26,
          "end": 76.02,
          "en": "if the navigation you're trying to trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.02,
          "end": 77.40299999999999,
          "en": "would be completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 81.27,
          "en": "Now here I only care about the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.27,
          "end": 84.633,
          "en": "but you could add all these other input parameters as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.07,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "Well, and since component is now that component instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "which I'm trying to leave, we could for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "access its properties and take a look at them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "And see if they contain any data that we might lose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 100.743,
          "en": "if we're navigating away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.85,
          "end": 106.85,
          "en": "So we can check if component entered title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 110.13,
          "en": "if we read that value, if it's truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.13,
          "end": 115.13,
          "en": "Or if component entered date is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.2,
          "end": 119.973,
          "en": "or if component entered summary is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 124.5,
          "en": "And if any of these properties is truthy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.5,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "it means that it contains data that was inserted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "by the user, and that in turn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 132.18,
          "en": "means that we might not want to navigate away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.18,
          "end": 134.343,
          "en": "At least not without asking.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.57,
          "end": 140.25,
          "en": "Now we can ask by calling window.confirm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.25,
          "end": 143.28,
          "en": "So the confirm method is a built-in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 145.2,
          "en": "that's provided by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.2,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "that will open a confirmation dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 151.65,
          "en": "where the user can choose yes or no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.65,
          "end": 154.95,
          "en": "And confirm will indeed return a boolean depending on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 157.863,
          "en": "whether the user did click yes or no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.91,
          "end": 161.73,
          "en": "In addition, confirm takes a message as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.73,
          "end": 164.493,
          "en": "that will be shown as part of that dialogue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.39,
          "end": 169.68,
          "en": "So here we could ask, do you really want to leave?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.68,
          "end": 174.68,
          "en": "You will lose the entered data, or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.49,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "And as a result, as mentioned, we get true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "And we can simply return that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "as part of this guard function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 187.14,
          "en": "If we're not inside of this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.14,
          "end": 191.283,
          "en": "so if we have unchanged data, we can instead return true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "So that then means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 197.19,
          "en": "that this guard function will always return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.19,
          "end": 199.98,
          "en": "if the user has not entered any values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.98,
          "end": 202.44,
          "en": "But if the user did enter values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.44,
          "end": 205.38,
          "en": "we'll ask the user and will return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.38,
          "end": 208.953,
          "en": "if the user chooses yes, and false otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.91,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "And if we return true, the user is allowed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 215.46,
          "en": "to leave the page and Angular will go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.46,
          "end": 218.79,
          "en": "and perform that upcoming navigation action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 221.823,
          "en": "Otherwise it will block it, essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "Though only if we register dysfunction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 229.23,
          "en": "as a can deactivate guard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.23,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "So with it defined here, we should go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 236.01,
          "en": "to our route definitions to this new task route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.01,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "And then there you can add the can deactivate property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 241.89,
          "en": "to this route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.89,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "And just like can match or can activate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 247.8,
          "en": "it takes an array of guards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.8,
          "end": 251.94,
          "en": "And here it's then this can leave added page guard function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.94,
          "end": 255.9,
          "en": "that you should add like this to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.9,
          "end": 258.42,
          "en": "And just as before, you shouldn't execute it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.42,
          "end": 260.313,
          "en": "You should just point at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 267.45,
          "en": "With that change made, if you are entering something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.45,
          "end": 269.91,
          "en": "and you click cancel, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 269.91,
          "end": 273.03,
          "en": "you see that you'll be prompted here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 273.03,
          "end": 276.093,
          "en": "and if you click cancel, you'll stay on this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.11,
          "end": 280.923,
          "en": "It's only if you click okay that you will be navigated away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 281.76,
          "end": 285.63,
          "en": "And that shows you how can deactivate works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 285.63,
          "end": 288.93,
          "en": "It allows you to add a guard that makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 288.93,
          "end": 292.11,
          "en": "that unintended page changes are prevented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.11,
          "end": 294.273,
          "en": "before they're even initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
